5\nL361: \nL362: #### Open Source\nL363: #### How Llama helps drive engineering efficiency at a major Australian bank\nL364: \nL365: ANZ, one of Australia's Big Four banks, is driving engineering efficiency with Llama.\nL366: \nL367: June 18, 2025\nL368: \nL369: cite31†Learn More L370: \nL371: Blog\nL372: \nL373: June 04, 2025\nL374: \nL375: #### Hardware\nL376: \nL377: #### Research\nL378: #### Inside Aria Gen 2: Explore the cutting-edge tech behind the device\nL379: \nL380: Today, we’re excited to share more about the technology inside Aria Gen 2. This includes an in-depth overview of the form factor, audio capabilities, battery life, upgraded cameras and sensors, on-device compute, and more.\nL381: \nL382: June 04, 2025\nL383: \nL384: cite32†Learn More L385: \nL386: Blog\nL387: \nL388: June 17, 2025\nL389: \nL390: #### Open Source\nL391: #### Announcing the inaugural Llama Startup Program cohort\nL392: \nL393: At Meta, we believe in the potential of early-stage startups to drive innovation in the generative AI market, and through the Llama Startup Program, we aim to lower the barrier to entry for getting started with Llama models.\nL394: \nL395: June 17, 2025\nL396: \nL397: cite33†Learn More L398: \nL399: Blog\nL400: \nL401: June 11, 2025\nL402: \nL403: #### Research\nL404: \nL405: #### Open Source\nL406: #### Introducing the V-JEPA 2 world model and new benchmarks for physical reasoning\nL407: \nL408: We’re excited to share V-JEPA 2, the first world model trained on video that enables state-of-the-art understanding and prediction, as well as zero-shot planning and robot control in new environments.\nL409: \nL410: June 11, 2025\nL411: \nL412: cite34†Learn More L413: \nL414: Blog\nL415: \nL416: May 14, 2025\nL417: \nL418: #### Open Source\nL419: #### Sharing new breakthroughs and artifacts supporting molecular property prediction, language processing, and neuroscience\nL420: \nL421: Meta FAIR is sharing new research artifacts that highlight our commitm